  $t$Run 42517 stopped at Panel Check: hydrogen, a panel judge, spent 65,533 of its 65,536 output tokens on reasoning and returned no text; the engine called it "an envelope this parser does not recognise"; and no reserve was free, because the one seat the engine looked at for the reserve (the fourth free seat) was JFL-moved, although other seats had accepted. One empty reply ended a paid run with no row. This ASK (A) makes the reserve the first seat after the panel that is neither JFL-moved nor time-removed, and (B) makes a reply whose content is not text fail with "returned no text: finish_reason ...; output tokens ... (reasoning ...); prompt tokens ...". No reasoning setting, model setting, order or alternate order is touched. (plan rev 0, ask629/w4/plan629.md md5 2d000472; Wall 11919, 11929)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 05:15 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's press "Write it" (05:14 CST; written, Wall 11971; audit 42086), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11975). Engine dc258730 to 066525aa, two nodes, two lines, 423 nodes; child aad0ad9c unchanged. Init Seats: panel_reserve is the first seat of the free list after the panel that is neither JFL-moved nor time-removed, or none; before, it was the fourth free seat or none. Panel Check envelope(): a choices reply whose message content is not a string throws "FAIL-CLOSED: seat <s> returned no text: finish_reason <f>; output tokens <n> (reasoning <r>); prompt tokens <p>. NO ROW IS WRITTEN.", placed just before the old generic throw, after every parse branch; a field not given prints "not given". IN PART, because it is shown offline only (t629, 39 PASS, 0 FAIL, by W4 and by W1): the base code reproduces the stored Init Seats of runs 42528, 42517, 42505 and 42373 and on each only the reserve changes, from none to qwen4max (42373, 42505) or sonnet (42517, 42528); with the fourth seat eligible the output is byte-equal to the old; with every later seat JFL-moved the reserve is still none; on the 42517 replay the old Panel Check throws as stored and the new one makes one substitution (slot 3, hydrogen to sonnet, kind no_usable_judgment, reason "empty reply") with the detail "returned no text: finish_reason length; output tokens 65,536 (reasoning 65,533); prompt tokens 75,848"; envelope() is byte-equal on nine other reply forms. FINDING of the build: every replayable live run since ASK 591 had no reserve, because the fourth free seat was JFL-moved. W1's R1 (a substituted reserve must not also sit as an alternate): met by the alternate guard G3, which refuses a model already on the panel; an unused reserve is still offered. NOT SHOWN: no live run since the write; W1 N2: the post-substitution payloads of R1 were built by hand; W1 N1: array content was refused before and still is, now under the new wording; W4 did not read the majority count code, which the change does not touch. The build was made on engine 2df7f6fa (b1, target 55d96341) and rebuilt on dc258730 after ASK 626 was written (b2, target 0e720823); W1 confirmed the rebase. Open: two clean live runs (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); the reserve path fires only when a panel judge fails. REVISION (this row): the engine manual is WRITTEN, part 10.0 v311 to v321 (438a0c8d, 63,057 characters) and part 16.0 v242 to v322 (e5639a54, 2,377), on the operator's press "Write it" at 05:47 CST 2026-11-25 on W3's card, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11983, 11984). objective_met stays 'in part': no live run since the engine write. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, EXERCISED. All three marks are shown. (1) The JUDGE ORDER line reads "SEATED: panel qwen4max, sol, sol62; reserve sonnet; alternates chatgpt, sonnet". (2) A panel judge returned no text and the failure names the cause: panel_substitution detail 'FAIL-CLOSED: seat "qwen4max" returned no text: finish_reason error; output tokens 28,911 (reasoning 28,911); prompt tokens 87,816. NO ROW IS WRITTEN.', reason "empty reply", failed_seat qwen4max, substitute sonnet. (3) The reserve judged: call_costs holds "Panel Reserve openrouter" (anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5) and judgment 1281 (sonnet) is stored whole. The substituted reserve was then refused as an alternate for sol and sol62 (the removal audit lines read that sonnet "already sits on this panel"). Outside this ASK: sonnet was later removed on one assumption item by a defect of the verse reader (ASK 672). NOT SHOWN: an alternate reply cut at its output limit (the case of run 42528 did not arise). W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks; objective_met stays 'in part' and status stays 'read back' until the second.$t$,
